chx:isCharacterizedBy a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "is characterized by"@en ;
    skos:altLabel "is signalled by"@en ;
    skos:altLabel "ran over"@en ;
    rdfs:domain owl:Thing ; rdfs:range owl:Thing ;
    kb:hasRelationshipCategory kb:RelationshipCategory_Characterization ;
    skos:definition "Links an example to the example of another section that illustrates a feature the first one carries and by which it is told from others: the service bit that marks a kind of node, the transport that a connection type spoke. It is not a requirement (the feature is not needed in order to work) and not a part (the feature is not a component)."@en ;
    rdfs:comment "No standard relation was reused: none of the standard properties checked says that a thing is told by a feature it carries without saying that it is part of it or needs it. The domain and the range are owl:Thing on purpose: the ends are examples of two different sections, and the six top classes of the taxonomy are pairwise disjoint, so no named class covers both ends (the rule BP-D23 for a property used across branches with no common ancestor). The class pair belongs to the link and to the sentence that states it. The shape of the domain shapes file checks that both ends are individuals of the chapter."@en ;
    dcterms:source "RELATIONSHIP_TAXONOMY_RESEARCH_v1_11_0.md of the OEE (OE v2.33.0), section 3, the category Characterization (a thing and its characteristic); construction method BP-D58."@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://example.org/sen0401/ch10/tbox> .
chx:isCountedIn a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "is counted in"@en ; rdfs:subPropertyOf <http://purl.org/dc/terms/isPartOf> ;
    rdfs:domain owl:Thing ; rdfs:range owl:Thing ;
    kb:hasRelationshipCategory kb:RelationshipCategory_ContainmentMembership ;
    skos:definition "Links an example to the example of another section that illustrates a count or a whole in which the first one is included: the nodes reached through an overlay network are among the nodes of the census. It joins a member and the collection it is counted in; no other property of the chapter says membership."@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Reused: dcterms:isPartOf says that a resource is included in another, which is what the sentences of both links say of the nodes of an overlay network and the census. The domain and the range are owl:Thing on purpose: the ends are examples of two different sections, and the six top classes of the taxonomy are pairwise disjoint, so no named class covers both ends (the rule BP-D23 for a property used across branches with no common ancestor). The class pair belongs to the link and to the sentence that states it. The shape of the domain shapes file checks that both ends are individuals of the chapter."@en ;
    dcterms:source "RELATIONSHIP_TAXONOMY_RESEARCH_v1_11_0.md of the OEE (OE v2.33.0), section 3, the category Containment and membership; construction method BP-D58."@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://example.org/sen0401/ch10/tbox> .
