    rdfs:label "comes before"@en ;
    skos:altLabel "came before"@en ;
    skos:altLabel "is earlier than"@en ;
    rdfs:domain owl:Thing ; rdfs:range owl:Thing ;
    kb:hasRelationshipCategory kb:RelationshipCategory_SuccessionTransformation ;
    skos:definition "Links an example to the example of another section that illustrates what comes after it in time: in the order of messages of a new connection the verack before the feefilter, the wtxidrelay before the announcement by wtxid, the sendcmpct before the choice of mode, the getheaders before the batch of headers, and the relay network of 2015 before the BIP of compact blocks of 2016. It says only that the first is earlier; it states no cause and no requirement."@en ;
    rdfs:comment "No standard relation was reused. BFO precedes (BFO_0000063) was reused in version 1.1.0 for these links; it joins occurrents, and the ends of the link of the relay network are examples that carry dates, so the statement was not true of every link and is withdrawn here, as in chapter 11 for OWL-Time's before. The domain and the range are owl:Thing on purpose: the ends are examples of two different sections, and the six top classes of the taxonomy are pairwise disjoint, so no named class covers both ends (the rule BP-D23 for a property used across branches with no common ancestor). The class pair belongs to the link and to the sentence that states it. The shape of the domain shapes file checks that both ends are individuals of the chapter."@en ;
    dcterms:source "RELATIONSHIP_TAXONOMY_RESEARCH_v1_11_0.md of the OEE (OE v2.33.0), section 3, the category Succession and transformation (direct sequence); construction method BP-D58."@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://example.org/sen0401/ch10/tbox> .
chx:buildsOn a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "builds on"@en ;
    skos:altLabel "needs"@en ;
    skos:altLabel "requires"@en ;
    skos:altLabel "is framed as described in"@en ; rdfs:subPropertyOf <http://purl.org/dc/terms/requires> ;
    rdfs:domain owl:Thing ; rdfs:range owl:Thing ;
    kb:hasRelationshipCategory kb:RelationshipCategory_Requirement ;
    skos:definition "Links an example to the example of another section that illustrates something the first one needs in order to work or to be defined: addrv2 needs the protocol version 70016, FIBRE needs compact blocks, a merkleblock needs the Merkle path, a light client needs the header chain checks, an addr-fetch connection needs the address exchange, the plain transport needs the frame of the old transport. It differs from takes part in (a participation is not a need) and from is a reason for (the needed thing is not the cause of the first)."@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Reused: dcterms:requires says that a resource is required by another to support its function or coherence, which is what the sentence of each of the six links says. The domain and the range are owl:Thing on purpose: the ends are examples of two different sections, and the six top classes of the taxonomy are pairwise disjoint, so no named class covers both ends (the rule BP-D23 for a property used across branches with no common ancestor). The class pair belongs to the link and to the sentence that states it. The shape of the domain shapes file checks that both ends are individuals of the chapter."@en ;
    dcterms:source "RELATIONSHIP_TAXONOMY_RESEARCH_v1_11_0.md of the OEE (OE v2.33.0), section 3, the category Requirement; construction method BP-D58."@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://example.org/sen0401/ch10/tbox> .
chx:takesPartIn a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "takes part in"@en ;
    rdfs:domain owl:Thing ; rdfs:range owl:Thing ;
    kb:hasRelationshipCategory kb:RelationshipCategory_Participation ;
    skos:definition "Links an example to the example of another section that illustrates a process or an exchange in which the first one takes part: the handling of an orphan transaction takes part in the announcement by wtxid. It differs from builds on in the category: the orphan is not shown to need the announcement in order to be defined, it is shown to be asked for through it."@en ;
    rdfs:comment "No standard relation was reused: dcterms:requires would say a need, which the sentence of the link does not state. The domain and the range are owl:Thing on purpose: the ends are examples of two different sections, and the six top classes of the taxonomy are pairwise disjoint, so no named class covers both ends (the rule BP-D23 for a property used across branches with no common ancestor). The class pair belongs to the link and to the sentence that states it. The shape of the domain shapes file checks that both ends are individuals of the chapter."@en ;
    dcterms:source "RELATIONSHIP_TAXONOMY_RESEARCH_v1_11_0.md of the OEE (OE v2.33.0), section 3, the category Participation; construction method BP-D58."@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://example.org/sen0401/ch10/tbox> .
chx:isMeansAgainst a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "is a means against"@en ;
    skos:altLabel "helps to defend against"@en ;
    skos:altLabel "is a means to shorten"@en ;
    rdfs:domain owl:Thing ; rdfs:range owl:Thing ;
    kb:hasRelationshipCategory kb:RelationshipCategory_Intentional ;
    skos:definition "Links an example to the example of another section that illustrates a harm or a loss which the first one is a means to lessen: the peers of other networks and the block-relay-only connections against the routing and the eclipse attack, the compact blocks against the chance that a rival block is found while a block travels. It states a purpose of the first, not a cause: it differs from is a reason for, which says why something exists."@en ;
    rdfs:comment "No standard relation was reused: none of the standard properties checked says that a thing is a means to lessen a harm. The domain and the range are owl:Thing on purpose: the ends are examples of two different sections, and the six top classes of the taxonomy are pairwise disjoint, so no named class covers both ends (the rule BP-D23 for a property used across branches with no common ancestor). The class pair belongs to the link and to the sentence that states it. The shape of the domain shapes file checks that both ends are individuals of the chapter."@en ;
    dcterms:source "RELATIONSHIP_TAXONOMY_RESEARCH_v1_11_0.md of the OEE (OE v2.33.0), section 3, the category Intentional relationship (means and end); construction method BP-D58."@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://example.org/sen0401/ch10/tbox> .
chx:replaces a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "replaces"@en ; rdfs:subPropertyOf <http://purl.org/dc/terms/replaces> ;
    rdfs:domain owl:Thing ; rdfs:range owl:Thing ;
    kb:hasRelationshipCategory kb:RelationshipCategory_Versioning ;
    skos:definition "Links an example to the example of another section that illustrates what it took the place of: the basic block filter of BIP 158 replaced the Bloom filter of BIP 37. It states a supersession, not an order in time only (it differs from comes before) and not a need (it differs from builds on)."@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Reused: dcterms:replaces says that a resource supplants, displaces or supersedes another, which is what the sentence of the link says. The domain and the range are owl:Thing on purpose: the ends are examples of two different sections, and the six top classes of the taxonomy are pairwise disjoint, so no named class covers both ends (the rule BP-D23 for a property used across branches with no common ancestor). The class pair belongs to the link and to the sentence that states it. The shape of the domain shapes file checks that both ends are individuals of the chapter."@en ;
    dcterms:source "RELATIONSHIP_TAXONOMY_RESEARCH_v1_11_0.md of the OEE (OE v2.33.0), section 3, the category Versioning; construction method BP-D58."@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://example.org/sen0401/ch10/tbox> .
chx:isComparedWith a owl:ObjectProperty, owl:SymmetricProperty ;
    rdfs:label "is compared with"@en ;
    skos:altLabel "differs from"@en ;
    skos:altLabel "is like"@en ;
    skos:altLabel "shares with"@en ;
    rdfs:domain owl:Thing ; rdfs:range owl:Thing ;
    kb:hasRelationshipCategory kb:RelationshipCategory_Comparative ;
    skos:definition "Links two examples of different sections when the account sets what they illustrate side by side, as alike or as different: the privacy of a block filter and of a Bloom filter, the SipHash of the filter and of the short ids, the guard of the memory by presync and by the orphanage, the withholding of transactions by the feefilter and by the relay flag, the mempool and the orphan pool as local views."@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Symmetric, so the link is stated once and holds both ways. No standard relation says a comparison. The domain and the range are owl:Thing on purpose: the ends are examples of two different sections, and the six top classes of the taxonomy are pairwise disjoint, so no named class covers both ends (the rule BP-D23 for a property used across branches with no common ancestor). The class pair belongs to the link and to the sentence that states it. The shape of the domain shapes file checks that both ends are individuals of the chapter."@en ;
    dcterms:source "RELATIONSHIP_TAXONOMY_RESEARCH_v1_11_0.md of the OEE (OE v2.33.0), section 3, the category Similarity and opposition (Comparative); construction method BP-D58."@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://example.org/sen0401/ch10/tbox> .
chx:isReasonFor a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "is a reason for"@en ;
    skos:altLabel "motivates"@en ;
    skos:altLabel "is the base of"@en ;
    rdfs:domain owl:Thing ; rdfs:range owl:Thing ;
    kb:hasRelationshipCategory kb:RelationshipCategory_Causal ;
    skos:definition "Links an example to the example of another section that illustrates what exists because of it: the five address formats of the five networks are the reason for addrv2, and the relay flag set to false is the base of the block-relay-only connections. It says why the second exists; it differs from is a means against, which states what the first is for."@en ;
    rdfs:comment "No standard relation was reused: the Relations Ontology could not be opened in this run, so none was checked against the account. The domain and the range are owl:Thing on purpose: the ends are examples of two different sections, and the six top classes of the taxonomy are pairwise disjoint, so no named class covers both ends (the rule BP-D23 for a property used across branches with no common ancestor). The class pair belongs to the link and to the sentence that states it. The shape of the domain shapes file checks that both ends are individuals of the chapter."@en ;
    dcterms:source "RELATIONSHIP_TAXONOMY_RESEARCH_v1_11_0.md of the OEE (OE v2.33.0), section 3, the category Causal relationship; construction method BP-D58."@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://example.org/sen0401/ch10/tbox> .
